      "widgets_values": [
        "cinemoraX, a velvet-draped office overlooking a post-apocalyptic city frozen in twilight, a skeletal lich sits calmly in a leather chair, legs crossed, holding a clipboard made of ancient bone and spider silk. Despite his corpse-like visage, he wears a tweed blazer patched with time — his hollow eye sockets glow gently as if warmed by empathy.\n\nAcross from him, a weeping chimera — half lion, half serpent — lies sprawled across a fainting couch, its massive paws clutching a pillow embroidered with runes of comfort. The air hums faintly with enchantments meant to suppress traumatic memories. Tattered tapestries hang on the walls, each one depicting failed hero quests and fallen kingdoms — reminders of the therapist’s past life as a destroyer.\n\nNow, the Lich listens.\n\nA clock made of gnashing teeth ticks backward. Candles flicker inside skull sconces, casting soft halos of irony. Bottles of spectral ink float beside a desk cluttered with dream journals. On a shelf, a potted mandrake curls into itself, soothed by the stillness."
      ],
